{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall speak to all who are wise of heart.</b> The word ועשו ('and they shall make') is joined to חכמי לב ('wise of heart') to hint that the making of the garments must come from a thought of wisdom — namely, that they required making them for their own sake (leshmah). And it says ועשית ('and you shall make') — that they be made with that intention. And you will find in this pericah three instances of לכהנו לי ('to minister to Me'), where it should have said לכהן לי ('to minister to Me'); and the three extra וי״ן allude to the 18 High Priests who served in the First Temple."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:58.826444681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}